<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21261] kernel update [RHEL 8.10 4.18.0-553.187.1.el8_10]</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21261</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Security Fix(es) for kernel 4.18.0-553.187.1.el8_10:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: proc: protect ptrace_may_access() with exec_update_lock (FD links) (CVE-2026-64375)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: Bluetooth: bpa10x: avoid OOB read of revision string in bpa10x_setup() (CVE-2026-64549)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: wifi: mwifiex: bound uAP association event IEs to the event buffer (CVE-2026-68326)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: wifi: mac80211: validate extension-frame layout before RX (CVE-2026-68470)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: net/smc: fix socket use-after-free during link group termination (CVE-2026-74493)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: wifi: mwifiex: use the subframe length when parsing A-MSDU TDLS frames (CVE-2026-74488)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: net: smc: fix splice entry lifetime imbalance in smc_rx_splice (CVE-2026-74631)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: perf/core: Fix group leader use-after-free after sibling detach (CVE-2026-74637)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: nvdimm/btt: reject an arena whose nfree is below the lane count (CVE-2026-89965)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: slip: remove slip_hangup() to fix use-after-free in slip_receive_buf() (CVE-2026-90057)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: scsi: qla2xxx: Unlink NVMe unsol ctx before freeing on LS reject error (CVE-2026-97528)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: RDMA/siw: Bound fragmented header copies by the remaining length (CVE-2026-98323)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: cipso: adjust cached option offsets when removing CIPSO (CVE-2026-99064)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Bug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s) for kernel 4.18.0-553.187.1.el8_10:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;RHEL-8&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; The slab cache entries for gfs2 and dlm grow very large for gfs2 filesystems (JIRA:RHEL-220529)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;XFS NULL pointer dereference in xfs_inode_mark_reclaimable due to race in xfs_free_perag during umount (JIRA:RHEL-247835)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kprobe/ftrace: use-after-free and panic after ftrace_kill(), needs backport of 1a7d0890dd4a and e113f0b46d19 (JIRA:RHEL-284885)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Critical Bug Fixes for customer issues with lpfc &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;rhel-8.10.z&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; (JIRA:RHEL-286158)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Backport CVEs from v7.2 &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;rhel-8.10.z&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; (JIRA:RHEL-300371)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Fix crasher in gss_unwrap_resp_integ() (JIRA:RHEL-309171)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://access.redhat.com/errata/product/479/ver=/rhel---8/x86_64/RHSA-2026:100730" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://access.redhat.com/errata/product/479/ver=/rhel---8/x86_64/RHSA-2026:100730&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
